WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:31.875
<b>Here, Krishna says</b>

2
00:00:31.875 --> 00:00:35.708
<b>that when a person has before</b>
<b>them a vast, overflowing lake,</b>

3
00:00:35.708 --> 00:00:40.208
<b>that lake alone is sufficient </b>
<b>to fulfill all their needs.</b>

4
00:00:40.208 --> 00:00:41.208
<b>In such a case,</b>

5
00:00:41.208 --> 00:00:46.291
<b>there is no need to think about </b>
<b>smaller water sources nearby.</b>

6
00:00:46.291 --> 00:00:47.291
<b>Similarly,</b>

7
00:00:47.291 --> 00:00:50.458
<b>when one attains the </b>
<b>knowledge of the Supreme Soul,</b>

8
00:00:50.458 --> 00:00:53.500
<b>that vast lake of wisdom is sufficient.</b>

9
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.666
<b>In its presence,</b>

10
00:00:54.666 --> 00:00:59.541
<b>there appears no need for </b>
<b>knowledge sources beyond the Vedas.</b>

11
00:01:04.416 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>Understand it this way</b>

12
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:13.083
<b>often in villages, people create </b>
<b>multiple water bodies for their various needs.</b>

13
00:01:13.083 --> 00:01:15.250
<b>One well for drinking water,</b>

14
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:18.666
<b>a small pool for bathing</b>

15
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:20.250
<b>and washing clothes,</b>

16
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.458
<b>another water body for animals,</b>

17
00:01:22.458 --> 00:01:25.875
<b>and other such water storages.</b>

18
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:26.666
<b>But</b>

19
00:01:26.666 --> 00:01:30.666
<b>if there's a vast flowing river right </b>
<b>in the middle of that village,</b>

20
00:01:30.666 --> 00:01:36.041
<b>all the villagers' needs can be fulfilled </b>
<b>at that riverbank alone.</b>

21
00:01:36.041 --> 00:01:37.125
<b>In such a case,</b>

22
00:01:37.125 --> 00:01:40.875
<b>there's no need for numerous </b>
<b>artificial water bodies.</b>

23
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.000
<b>Similarly,</b>

24
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.541
<b>while the Vedas contain</b>
<b>many sources of knowledge,</b>

25
00:01:44.541 --> 00:01:48.833
<b>Nishkama Karma Yoga (selfless action)</b>
<b>is such a vast source </b>

26
00:01:48.833 --> 00:01:52.375
<b>that it's sufficient for satisfying the soul's thirst.</b>

27
00:01:52.375 --> 00:01:55.875
<b>Once Nishkama Karma Yoga is embraced in life,</b>

28
00:01:55.875 --> 00:02:04.500
<b>there remains no need for any of those rituals </b>
<b>and procedures that the ignorant rely upon.</b>

29
00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.791
<b>Understand it this way too</b>

30
00:02:06.791 --> 00:02:10.833
<b>a student enters a new class each year,</b>

31
00:02:10.833 --> 00:02:13.500
<b>gains knowledge of new subjects,</b>

32
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:18.333
<b>this is a process that continues year after year.</b>

33
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:21.625
<b>But what is the supreme </b>
<b>purpose of this process?</b>

34
00:02:21.625 --> 00:02:26.666
<b>Isn't it that the student, upon completing</b>
<b>their education, becomes independent,</b>

35
00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:28.291
<b>becomes a good citizen,</b>

36
00:02:28.291 --> 00:02:31.375
<b>and becomes capable of living life?</b>

37
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:32.541
<b>Similarly,</b>

38
00:02:32.541 --> 00:02:36.750
<b>within the Vedas too there</b>
<b>are many classes, many subjects</b>

39
00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:42.166
<b>there is knowledge related to the three </b>
<b>qualities of Sattva, Rajas, and Tamas,</b>

40
00:02:42.166 --> 00:02:46.125
<b>but the supreme purpose of all these is one:</b>

41
00:02:46.125 --> 00:02:50.791
<b>that humans ultimately become </b>
<b>capable of uniting with God.</b>

42
00:02:50.791 --> 00:02:53.458
<b>And for achieving this supreme purpose,</b>

43
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:58.875
<b>Nishkama Karma Yoga </b>
<b>alone is completely sufficient.</b>

44
00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:07.083
<b>Being spiritually aware</b>

45
00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:10.833
<b>and being fanatical about </b>
<b>spirituality and religion</b>

46
00:03:10.833 --> 00:03:15.500
<b>there is a world of difference </b>
<b>between these two.</b>

47
00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:20.583
<b>An aware person understands the </b>
<b>fundamental meaning of teachings,</b>

48
00:03:20.583 --> 00:03:23.875
<b>grasps the essence of any spiritual practice.</b>

49
00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:27.250
<b>If a practice elevates you,</b>

50
00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:30.666
<b>brings positive changes within you</b>

51
00:03:30.666 --> 00:03:34.333
<b>this indicates awareness.</b>

52
00:03:34.333 --> 00:03:35.541
<b>But</b>

53
00:03:35.541 --> 00:03:41.041
<b>if you're performing a practice </b>
<b>merely as a daily routine,</b>

54
00:03:41.041 --> 00:03:45.083
<b>and your goal is neither self-reflection</b>

55
00:03:45.083 --> 00:03:46.500
<b>nor improvement,</b>

56
00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:51.541
<b>then it remains merely a show.</b>

57
00:03:51.541 --> 00:03:53.375
<b>Moreover,</b>

58
00:03:53.375 --> 00:04:00.500
<b>if you focus more on others' faults </b>
<b>than your own improvement,</b>

59
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:06.291
<b>discuss others' beliefs more than self-reflection,</b>

60
00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:12.291
<b>try to harm others under the guise of religion </b>

61
00:04:12.291 --> 00:04:17.625
<b>this surely indicates your fanaticism.</b>

62
00:04:17.625 --> 00:04:21.750
<b>This is entirely inappropriate.</b>

63
00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:30.791
<b>The purpose of spiritual knowledge is </b>
<b>to make your perspective broad, not narrow.</b>

64
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:34.666
<b>Its purpose is to elevate you,</b>

65
00:04:34.666 --> 00:04:38.291
<b>not to find faults in others.</b>

66
00:04:38.291 --> 00:04:40.666
<b>Be aware,</b>

67
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:42.208
<b>not fanatical.</b>

68
00:04:47.041 --> 00:04:49.791
<b>In current social conditions,</b>

69
00:04:49.791 --> 00:04:51.291
<b>many people</b>

70
00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:56.041
<b>mistakenly consider fanaticism to be right.</b>

71
00:04:56.041 --> 00:05:00.208
<b>They believe that only their path is correct,</b>

72
00:05:00.208 --> 00:05:02.458
<b>only their thoughts are right.</b>

73
00:05:02.458 --> 00:05:08.208
<b>And whoever thinks differently is wrong.</b>

74
00:05:08.208 --> 00:05:15.458
<b>Such narrow thinking leaves no room </b>
<b>for diverse streams of thought,</b>

75
00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:20.750
<b>and this often becomes the cause of conflict.</b>

76
00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.208
<b>But</b>

77
00:05:23.208 --> 00:05:28.291
<b>if one understands the true meaning of </b>
<b>religion and spirituality,</b>

78
00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:30.166
<b>they'll know</b>

79
00:05:30.166 --> 00:05:37.541
<b>that the purpose of both is simply to</b>
<b>help the soul regain its lost knowledge,</b>

80
00:05:37.541 --> 00:05:42.833
<b>to restore the soul's lost dignity. </b>

81
00:05:42.833 --> 00:05:45.625
<b>Take the example of a journey</b>

82
00:05:45.625 --> 00:05:47.375
<b>you're traveling somewhere,</b>

83
00:05:47.375 --> 00:05:50.291
<b>everyone on the road has different vehicles,</b>

84
00:05:50.291 --> 00:05:51.625
<b>some are fast,</b>

85
00:05:51.625 --> 00:05:53.125
<b>some are slow.</b>

86
00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:54.958
<b>Some have gone ahead of you,</b>

87
00:05:54.958 --> 00:05:57.500
<b>some are behind.</b>

88
00:05:57.500 --> 00:05:58.333
<b>But</b>

89
00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:01.291
<b>what difference does this make?</b>

90
00:06:01.291 --> 00:06:04.916
<b>The purpose of the journey is one, isn't it</b>

91
00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:09.333
<b>to reach one's destination?</b>

92
00:06:09.333 --> 00:06:18.791
<b>Everyone will reach their destination in their own</b>
<b>vehicles, at their own pace, by their own paths.</b>

93
00:06:18.791 --> 00:06:21.250
<b>This is not a competition</b>

94
00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:23.750
<b>where one's victory</b>

95
00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:27.583
<b>means another's defeat.</b>

96
00:06:27.583 --> 00:06:29.625
<b>Similarly,</b>

97
00:06:29.625 --> 00:06:33.875
<b>every person has their own spiritual journey,</b>

98
00:06:33.875 --> 00:06:40.375
<b>where everyone's speed, path, </b>
<b>and vehicle are different.</b>

99
00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:46.416
<b>You too must focus on your journey, </b>
<b>your destination.</b>

100
00:06:46.416 --> 00:06:50.708
<b>When everyone understands </b>
<b>religion from this perspective,</b>

101
00:06:50.708 --> 00:06:59.541
<b>diverse ideologies will surely coexist </b>
<b>in society with mutual respect.</b>

102
00:06:59.541 --> 00:07:02.750
<b>Make your perspective broad,</b>

103
00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.500
<b>not narrow.</b>

104
00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:09.708
<b>If you can help someone on</b>
<b>this journey, certainly do so.</b>

105
00:07:09.708 --> 00:07:10.916
<b>But</b>

106
00:07:10.916 --> 00:07:17.791
<b>if you've begun to think others </b>
<b>are wrong and only you are right,</b>

107
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:21.333
<b>this is surely a sign of fanaticism.</b>

108
00:07:21.333 --> 00:07:24.500
<b>This is entirely inappropriate.</b>

109
00:07:29.291 --> 00:07:34.958
<b>Any professional organization is </b>
<b>a congregation of diverse people.</b>

110
00:07:34.958 --> 00:07:37.166
<b>Everyone has their own nature,</b>

111
00:07:37.166 --> 00:07:38.625
<b>their own tendencies,</b>

112
00:07:38.625 --> 00:07:40.791
<b>their own work pace,</b>

113
00:07:40.791 --> 00:07:42.708
<b>and so on.</b>

114
00:07:42.708 --> 00:07:49.708
<b>Many people are full of enthusiasm when </b>
<b>they begin working in an organization,</b>

115
00:07:49.708 --> 00:07:53.416
<b>but amidst such diversity, after some time</b>

116
00:07:53.416 --> 00:07:57.583
<b>they feel confused.</b>

117
00:07:57.583 --> 00:08:00.333
<b>Why does this happen?</b>

118
00:08:00.333 --> 00:08:03.125
<b>Perhaps this happens because</b>

119
00:08:03.125 --> 00:08:09.791
<b>they've forgotten their initial purpose.</b>

120
00:08:09.791 --> 00:08:17.291
<b>To fulfill their work and duty with</b>
<b>complete capability and honesty,</b>

121
00:08:17.291 --> 00:08:22.666
<b>wasn't this their initial purpose?</b>

122
00:08:22.666 --> 00:08:27.541
<b>This purpose was the source of </b>
<b>their abundant enthusiasm,</b>

123
00:08:27.541 --> 00:08:34.250
<b>but after some time they unknowingly </b>
<b>get entangled in many questions.</b>

124
00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:36.375
<b>Whom to keep happy,</b>

125
00:08:36.375 --> 00:08:38.416
<b>what is whose nature,</b>

126
00:08:38.416 --> 00:08:45.375
<b>what might offend whom, </b>
<b>who is it that they don't like,</b>

127
00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:46.291
<b>and</b>

128
00:08:46.291 --> 00:08:50.250
<b>in trying to balance such many things,</b>

129
00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:56.125
<b>they forget their initial purpose.</b>

130
00:08:56.125 --> 00:09:02.916
<b>Don't change your direction </b>
<b>or pace by looking at others.</b>

131
00:09:02.916 --> 00:09:09.000
<b>Whenever you feel defeated or </b>
<b>indifferent at the workplace,</b>

132
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:16.958
<b>try to remember what your purpose</b>
<b>was when you started working here,</b>

133
00:09:16.958 --> 00:09:19.666
<b>why you were enthusiastic.</b>

134
00:09:19.666 --> 00:09:27.791
<b>Focus on this, and once again engage</b>
<b>in your work with full capacity.</b>

135
00:09:27.791 --> 00:09:34.916
<b>When you remember your </b>
<b>purpose again and focus on it,</b>

136
00:09:34.916 --> 00:09:39.666
<b>many dilemmas will resolve themselves.</b>

